% Test cases for the support surfaces policy (support_surfaces.le):
% synthetic claims, one or two per criterion of LCDs L33830 (Group 1),
% L33642 (Group 2) and L33692 (Group 3) and per payment condition of the
% Policy Articles, each stating only what its record shows. Findings are
% recorded as the treating practitioner's or the Council's; a finding
% nobody made leaves the answer conditional. The queries: whether the claim
% is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it
% is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal change would make it
% payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base support surfaces cases includes these resources:
    support_surfaces.

the knowledge base support surfaces cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete Group 1 claim: a foam mattress (E0184) purchased for a
% beneficiary who is completely immobile (criterion 1); the order, delivery
% and proof of delivery (E0184 needs neither a face-to-face encounter nor
% prior authorization).
scenario group_1_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the foam mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the foam mattress is "E0184".
    the foam mattress is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    Ann cannot make changes in body position without assistance.
    the order for the foam mattress is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the foam mattress is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the foam mattress includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the foam mattress includes order date.
    the order for the foam mattress includes description of the item.
    the order for the foam mattress includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the foam mattress includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the foam mattress was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the foam mattress was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the foam mattress.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Group 1 criterion 2: limited mobility with urinary incontinence, for a
% powered overlay (E0181).
scenario group_1_limited_mobility is:
    claim 1 is for the powered overlay.
    the HCPCS code of the powered overlay is "E0181".
    the powered overlay is furnished to Ben.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ben cannot independently make changes in body position significant enough to alleviate pressure.
    the medical record of Ben documents urinary incontinence.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same limited mobility without any of the conditions A-D: not
% reasonable and necessary.
scenario group_1_no_condition is:
    claim 1 is for the powered overlay.
    the HCPCS code of the powered overlay is "E0181".
    the powered overlay is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ben cannot independently make changes in body position significant enough to alleviate pressure.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Group 1 criterion 3: a stage 2 ulcer with altered sensory perception — on
% the pelvis (claim 1, covered) and on the heel (claim 2, not on the trunk
% or pelvis).
scenario group_1_ulcer_site is:
    claim 1 is for the foam overlay.
    the HCPCS code of the foam overlay is "E0199".
    the foam overlay is furnished to Cy.
    Cy has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 2 on pelvis.
    the medical record of Cy documents altered sensory perception.
    claim 2 is for the air overlay.
    the HCPCS code of the air overlay is "E0197".
    the air overlay is furnished to Dee.
    Dee has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 2 on heel.
    the medical record of Dee documents altered sensory perception.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A complete Group 2 claim: a powered mattress (E0277), first rental month,
% by criterion 1 — three stage 2 ulcers on the trunk and pelvis that failed
% to improve over six weeks of a comprehensive treatment program with every
% element; the order, the prior authorization (E0277 is on the required
% list), delivery and proof of delivery.
scenario group_2_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the powered mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the powered mattress is "E0277".
    the powered mattress is furnished to Eve.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Eve has 2 pressure ulcers of stage 2 on pelvis.
    Eve has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 2 on trunk.
    the pressure ulcers of Eve failed to improve over the past month.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve began on 2026-03-20.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve includes use of an appropriate group 1 support surface.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve includes regular assessment by a licensed healthcare practitioner.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve includes appropriate turning and positioning.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve includes appropriate wound care.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve includes appropriate management of moisture and incontinence.
    the comprehensive ulcer treatment program of Eve includes nutritional assessment and intervention.
    the order for the powered mattress is dated 2026-04-20.
    the order for the powered mattress is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the powered mattress includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the powered mattress includes order date.
    the order for the powered mattress includes description of the item.
    the order for the powered mattress includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the powered mattress includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the powered mattress was communicated to the supplier on 2026-04-22.
    prior authorization for the powered mattress was affirmed on 2026-04-25.
    the powered mattress was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the powered mattress.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

