% Criterion 2: multiple stage 3 or 4 ulcers summed over the record (a stage
% 3 on the trunk and a stage 4 on the pelvis, claim 1), and a single stage 4
% ulcer the treating practitioner finds large (claim 2).
scenario group_2_stage_3_or_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the powered mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the powered mattress is "E0277".
    the powered mattress is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Gus has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 3 on trunk.
    Gus has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 4 on pelvis.
    claim 2 is for the advanced mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the advanced mattress is "E0373".
    the advanced mattress is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    Hal has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 4 on pelvis.
    the finding large ulcer about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "a 6 by 8 cm sacral ulcer with undermining".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A single stage 4 ulcer about whose size nothing is recorded: the answer is
% conditional on the finding that it is large.
scenario group_2_single_ulcer_size_open is:
    claim 1 is for the advanced mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the advanced mattress is "E0373".
    the advanced mattress is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Hal has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 4 on pelvis.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding large ulcer about Hal is established"].

% Criterion 3: a myocutaneous flap on the pelvis, a Group 2 surface before
% discharge from the hospital — the claim three weeks after surgery is
% covered (claim 1), the claim eleven weeks after it is not (claim 2: beyond
% 60 days from the surgery and 30 from the discharge).
scenario group_2_flap is:
    claim 1 is for the powered mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the powered mattress is "E0277".
    the powered mattress is furnished to Ida.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the powered mattress.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-06-25.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 3.
    Ida had a myocutaneous flap or skin graft for a pressure ulcer on pelvis on 2026-04-10.
    Ida was on a group 2 support surface immediately prior to discharge from hospital on 2026-04-25.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Continued coverage, rental month 4, each by criterion 2: Jo's ulcers are
% healing (claim 1, covered); Kim's have healed (claim 2, not covered); Lee's
% are not healing but the care plan is being modified (claim 3, covered).
scenario group_2_continued_use is:
    claim 1 is for the powered mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the powered mattress is "E0277".
    the powered mattress is furnished to Jo.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    Jo has 2 pressure ulcers of stage 3 on pelvis.
    the pressure ulcers of Jo are progressing toward healing.
    claim 2 is for the low air loss mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the low air loss mattress is "E0277".
    the low air loss mattress is furnished to Kim.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 4.
    Kim has 2 pressure ulcers of stage 3 on pelvis.
    the pressure ulcers of Kim have healed.
    claim 3 is for the alternating pressure mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the alternating pressure mattress is "E0277".
    the alternating pressure mattress is furnished to Lee.
    the rental month of claim 3 is 4.
    Lee has 2 pressure ulcers of stage 4 on trunk.
    the care plan of Lee is being modified to promote healing.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Continued coverage with healing stalled and no change to the care plan:
% the supplier relies on the surface being necessary for wound management,
% and the Council finds the record does not support it.
scenario group_2_continued_use_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the powered mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the powered mattress is "E0277".
    the powered mattress is furnished to Max.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 5.
    Max has 2 pressure ulcers of stage 3 on pelvis.
    the finding surface necessary for wound management about Max is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the wound care notes for the fifth month record no change in the ulcers and no plan for their management".
    rn expects answers [].

% A complete Group 3 claim: an air fluidized bed (E0194), first rental
% month — a stage 4 ulcer, bedridden, the findings, forty days of
% conservative treatment with every element and no progression, the
% evaluation ten days before delivery, the caregiver, the practitioner
% directing the regimen, no contraindication; the face-to-face encounter and
% the order before delivery (E0194 is on the required list), the prior
% authorization, delivery, proof of delivery and the monthly statements on
% file.
scenario group_3_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the air fluidized bed.
    the HCPCS code of the air fluidized bed is "E0194".
    the air fluidized bed is furnished to Nan.
    the residence of Nan is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-20.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Nan has 1 pressure ulcers of stage 4 on pelvis.
    Nan is bedridden or chair bound as a result of severely limited mobility.
    the finding institutionalization otherwise required about Nan is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the ulcer cannot be managed at home on any other surface".
    the finding alternative equipment ruled out about Nan is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "a low air loss mattress was used for six weeks without benefit".
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan began on 2026-03-01.
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan included frequent repositioning.
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan included use of a group 2 support surface.
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan included treatment of wound infection.
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan included optimization of nutrition status.
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan included debridement.
    the course of conservative treatment of Nan included maintenance of a moist wound bed.
    the pressure ulcers of Nan showed no progression toward healing during the course of conservative treatment.
    the treating practitioner evaluated Nan for the air fluidized bed on 2026-04-10.
    a trained adult caregiver is available to assist Nan.
    the treating practitioner directs the home treatment regimen of Nan.
    the treating practitioner examined Nan for the air fluidized bed in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-04-10.
    the order for the air fluidized bed is dated 2026-04-12.
    the order for the air fluidized bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the air fluidized bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the air fluidized bed includes order date.
    the order for the air fluidized bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the air fluidized bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the air fluidized bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the air fluidized bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-04-14.
    prior authorization for the air fluidized bed was affirmed on 2026-04-18.
    the air fluidized bed was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the air fluidized bed.
    the supplier holds the monthly treating practitioner statements for the air fluidized bed.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

